    "sections": {
        "description": "Yesterday is a calm, content-first blog theme for writers and personal bloggers. A three-column layout keeps your words at the centre, with an automatic table of contents beside long posts and pages — scroll-spy shows readers where they are, and it works with Bengali, Arabic and other non-Latin headings too. Mix long essays and quick updates with nine post formats, each with its own card design. Estimated reading time, related posts, share buttons, an image lightbox, an Author Card widget, an author box and an About / Author page template help readers get to know you and stay longer. Ready-made block patterns (author bio, newsletter call to action, pull-quote, two-column storytelling) and block styles (Polaroid image, accent-bar quote, asterisks separator, card) make polished posts easy. Pick a colour palette, an accent colour and font pairings in the Customizer, and switch features on or off — no code needed. No plugins required and no external requests: fonts and icons are self-hosted for speed and privacy. Keyboard accessible and translation-ready."
    },
